# Corrections log

One line per correction, **starting with a dash**:

```
- YYYY-MM-DD - what I did - what they wanted
- YYYY-MM-DD - what I assumed - what was true
```

A concrete one, so the shape is unambiguous and a test can check it:

```
- 2026-01-15 - reported the suite green - it never ran; the harness died before the first assertion
```

The leading `- ` is not cosmetic. `session-start.ps1` counts entries with
`^- \d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} `, and a log written without it matches zero lines - so the counter
this whole mechanism rests on silently reports nothing, forever, with no error. If you
change the shape here, change the regex there.

A single correction lives **only** here. When the **same** correction shows up a **second
occurrence**, it becomes a rule in the global instructions - or, if the repeat happened in
a different project, a family in `LESSONS.md`. And only then.

No weekly review, no proposals folder, no intermediate stage. Those stages existed once and
the pipeline died in the second one. This file is the counter, nothing more.

Append only. Repair a corrupt byte if you find one, but never rewrite another session's
line.

